{"ts": "2026-10-27T06:00:32.750069Z", "run_id": "r-20261027T0558Z-d4a7", "unit": "openspec:proxy-budget-check", "seq": 21, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-002", "id": "Q-002", "status": "answered", "reason": "The question asks whether the inferred privileges of mintkey_app on budget_counters hold. I read 019-grants-defensive.yaml (default privileges plus runAlways blanket GRANT on all public tables, REVOKE only on audit_events), the compose Liquibase job (runs as mintkey_migrate, so the table created by 029 inherits the default privileges), the compose admin-api and proxy-plugin services (both connect as mintkey_app), and admin-api's permissions.py, which already inserts, updates and selects budget_counters as that role. No changeset revokes anything on budget_counters. The repository settles it; no business decision is involved.", "called": true, "tasks": ["1.1"], "target": null, "kind": "ambiguous", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.5077975, "decision": "answer", "answer_sha256": "b839ae64685e9454902729d03200cc7a48558e0a591fa58edaeb84e3f42e856a", "checked": [{"ref": "apps/admin-api/db/changelog/019-grants-defensive.yaml:28", "quote": "ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES IN SCHEMA public GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON TABLES TO mintkey_app;", "claim": "Tables later created in schema public by the migration role get SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE for mintkey_app by default."}, {"ref": "apps/admin-api/db/changelog/019-grants-defensive.yaml:19", "quote": "runAlways: true", "claim": "The defensive grant changeset re-runs on every Liquibase apply, so its blanket GRANT on all public tables also covers budget_counters after it exists."}, {"ref": "apps/admin-api/db/changelog/019-grants-defensive.yaml:26", "quote": "GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA public TO mintkey_app;", "claim": "Every public table, including budget_counters, is granted to mintkey_app on each apply."}, {"ref": "apps/admin-api/db/changelog/019-grants-defensive.yaml:33", "quote": "REVOKE UPDATE, DELETE ON audit_events FROM mintkey_app;", "claim": "The only revoke against mintkey_app targets audit_events, not budget_counters."}, {"ref": "apps/admin-api/db/changelog/029-budget-counters.yaml:13", "quote": "tableName: budget_counters", "claim": "budget_counters is created in schema public by the Liquibase changelog, after changeset 019 in the master order."}, {"ref": "apps/admin-api/db/changelog/db.changelog-master.yaml:57", "quote": "file: 019-grants-defensive.yaml", "claim": "Changeset 019 is included before 029-budget-counters in the master changelog."}, {"ref": "infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:100", "quote": "- --username=mintkey_migrate", "claim": "Liquibase runs the whole changelog as one role, so the default privileges set in 019 apply to the table created in 029."}, {"ref": "infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:263", "quote": "DATABASE_URL: postgresql+asyncpg://mintkey_app:mintkey_app_password@postgres:5432/mintkey", "claim": "admin-api connects to Postgres as mintkey_app."}, {"ref": "apps/admin-api/src/admin_api/api/permissions.py:686", "quote": "\"INSERT INTO budget_counters\"", "claim": "admin-api already inserts into budget_counters as mintkey_app, with ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE on the following lines."}, {"ref": "apps/admin-api/src/admin_api/api/permissions.py:1140", "quote": "\"UPDATE budget_counters SET used = 0\"", "claim": "admin-api already updates budget_counters as mintkey_app."}, {"ref": "infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:520", "quote": "DATABASE_URL: postgres://mintkey_app:mintkey_app_password@postgres:5432/mintkey", "claim": "The proxy-plugin uses the same mintkey_app role in compose."}, {"ref": "apps/proxy-plugin/internal/budget/budget.go:74", "quote": "INSERT INTO budget_counters (permission_id, period_start, period_end, ceiling, used, tenant_id)", "claim": "The proxy's counter statement needs INSERT and UPDATE on budget_counters, which the grants above give."}, {"ref": "spec:proposal.md", "quote": "Its role (`mintkey_app` in compose) needs `SELECT` on `permission_grants` and `SELECT`,\n  `INSERT`, `UPDATE` on `budget_counters`, which the existing grants give it.", "claim": "The proposal states the same conclusion that the changelogs confirm."}]}
